target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestDecide'
expect: push with -u
why:    the first push of a new feature branch is the NORMAL case, not a block — Step 14 pushes it with `-u origin`. The old "don't infer an upstream" rule blocked every fresh branch, which meant the gate's most common verdict was a refusal an operator had to override by hand, and a gate overridden by habit is not a gate.
--- old
	where := "feature branch with upstream"
	if !s.UpstreamExists {
		where = "feature branch has no upstream yet — push with -u"
	}
--- new
	where := "feature branch with upstream"
